Code Modernization — unofficial adaptation

The current package version is recorded in package.json. Version numbers in the
modification history below refer to earlier package states, not the current version.

This package is derived from Code Modernization by Anthropic:
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official/tree/main/plugins/code-modernization
Upstream manifest version inspected: 1.0.0. Sources inspected: 2026-10-15 (main).
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0; included in LICENSE.

Original authorship and attribution belong to Anthropic and the upstream contributors.
This is not an official Anthropic or OpenAI distribution and is not endorsed by them.

Modified files: all command/skill and agent Markdown files in this port are adaptations.
Changes: Claude-specific invocation, tools, workflow runtime and hooks are replaced with
Codex skills, explicit role instructions and foreground delegation. Python utilities and
telemetry are not distributed. Reports were initially written through host file tools;
0.6.0 adds the Node renderer and local browser interface described below.
See docs/UPSTREAM.md for the scope and provenance of these changes.
No test result obtained by the original Claude plugin is claimed for this port.

Additional modifications in 0.3.0 (2026-10-15): executable workflow adapters using the
public official Codex SDK APIs; Node.js command entry points, JSON schemas, plain-file
run state, tests and SDK-specific skills/documentation. These new files are port-specific,
not copies of an OpenAI runtime. The separately installed @openai/codex-sdk retains its
own distribution and license. No SDK binary or npm package is bundled in this archive.

Additional modifications in 0.4.0 (2026-10-15): input freshness and write-scope fixes,
command-evidenced unit test gates, partial-result propagation, native Node observation
comparison following the documented byte-mask/decimal constraints of upstream compare.py,
regression tests and reproducible npm dependencies. The original Python proof engine
and regex-mask semantics were not reproduced in that version.

Additional modifications in 0.5.0 (2026-10-15): Node ports of scripts/proof_pack.py,
baseline_diff.py, trace_rules.py and uplift_checks.py from upstream commit
c8874f5ad883e26428f483ffa4d537cc81489e64, in runtime/proof-*.mjs. These files are
modified translations of Anthropic's Apache-2.0 code. scripts/proof-pack.mjs provides
the positional CLI; verification skills use the deterministic Node evaluator.
runtime/regex-mask.mjs implements a bounded Python-compatible Latin-1 regex subset.
tests/fixtures/proof-pack-upstream.json.gz contains inputs and expected decisions
derived from upstream scripts/tests/test_proof_tools.py and test_proof_rules_run.py;
the Node tests replay them without a Python dependency. The upstream authors retain
their copyright and attribution. No test result of this port is an Anthropic endorsement.
The separately installed saxes and xmlchars retain their own licenses; their packages
are not vendored in this source distribution.

Additional modifications in 0.6.0 (2026-10-15): runtime/ui/upstream contains 21 adapted
plain-function modules from hooks/reader, hooks/review, hooks/map, hooks/fleet, hooks/xray,
hooks/paths.ts, hooks/text.ts and hooks/sign.ts at the same pinned Anthropic commit.
TypeScript types were erased and ESM import extensions added; system identifiers in
text.mjs follow this port's runtime contract. Claude-specific JSX and hook registration
are replaced by the browser UI in assets/panel.* and a foreground loopback Node service.
assets/report-template.html is the original template, adapted for Codex/demo labeling and sandboxed-frame navigation;
runtime/ui/report.mjs, proof-view.mjs and equivalence-view.mjs adapt build_report.py's
artifact projection and offline rendering. The source authors retain their attribution.
assets/vendor/mermaid.min.js is the upstream bundled Mermaid distribution; its MIT license
is included at assets/vendor/LICENSE-mermaid.txt. New local decision controls, revision
checks, SDK cancellation, synthetic examples and UI tests are port-specific changes.

Additional modifications in 0.7.0 (2026-10-15): authenticated SSE, revision/replay protocol,
bounded incremental journal tails and caches, keyed browser updates, workspace-scoped
drafts, document state preservation, runner health/queue/budgets, cooperative pause/resume,
explicit saved-run retry controls and concurrent human review with decision checkpoints.
These additions are original to this unofficial port; they are not Claude host hooks.

Additional modifications in 0.7.1 (2026-10-15): real installed-plugin self-assessment;
LRU eviction of idle live subscriptions with active/read pinning; preserved explicit
SDK/CLI locations on panel recovery; original cancellation/timeout diagnostics;
installation instructions verified with the local Codex CLI.
Report size units now distinguish source bytes/files from mapped lines/modules; unmapped dependencies remain unknown.

Additional modifications in 0.8.0 (2026-10-16): Node adaptations of make_shards.py and
render_rules.py; executable rule consolidation, selective security follow-ups and portfolio
metrics; Codex lifecycle hooks, managed panel lifetime/preferences, supported read X-ray,
parent/SDK test observations and recovered-command Fleet warnings. tests/fixtures/upstream-stacks.mjs
adapts Anthropic tests/fixtures/stacks.ts at c8874f5ad883e26428f483ffa4d537cc81489e64.
tests/fixtures/upstream-workspace.mjs likewise adapts tests/fixtures/workspace.ts from
that commit. The original fixture authors retain their attribution. These hook APIs belong to Codex;
native Claude terminal docking/prompt controls are not reproduced.

Advanced regex masks use separately installed @stephen-riley/pcre2-wasm 1.2.4 (MIT),
including its bundled PCRE2 WebAssembly and original licenses. No Python runtime is used.
runtime/latin1-names.mjs derives character names/aliases for U+0000..U+00FF from Unicode
16.0.0 UnicodeData.txt and NameAliases.txt, https://www.unicode.org/Public/16.0.0/ucd/.
Unicode License V3 is included at assets/vendor/UNICODE-LICENSE.txt.
